Research decision memo — Stage 0
Title: Optimizing Heterogeneous-Agent General Equilibrium
Status: NOT STARTED

Central hypothesis: Can a canonical incomplete-markets heterogeneous-agent economy satisfy individual optimization, rational expectations and general equilibrium with sufficiently accurate numerical solutions?

Feasibility prior:
Baseline: established in standard Aiyagari/Huggett-type economies, subject to the specified asset and aggregate-risk closure.

Core economic distinction:
Canonical representative-agent or no-idiosyncratic-risk economy under the same primitives

Conditions to check:
1. Household Bellman and Euler equations
2. Household budget and borrowing constraints
3. Goods, labor and bond/capital market clearing
4. Rational aggregate transition law

Pass / fail criterion:
Accept a fully converged and economically closed baseline; do not add nominal rigidity yet.

The project reports negative feasibility results when a kinetic, entropy, adaptive-trading, or heuristic-firm mechanism cannot be reconciled with optimization and equilibrium. Do not silently weaken rational expectations or drop clearing equations.

Evidence status: no derived theorems, numerical solutions or validated simulations committed yet.
